{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "Grappler",

  "_comment": "The second character, and the one that proves the system generalises (03 Game Design/Roster Plan.md). One character proves nothing — everything could be hardcoded to it. The pair is chosen to stress opposite parts of the engine: the Shoto is projectiles and invincibility, this is throw targeting, armour states and walk-speed balance. Placeholder numbers, legible rather than balanced, same as its counterpart.",

  "health": 11000,

  "_comment_walk": "Slower on the ground in both directions, which is the whole of what makes the archetype a problem to play: closing distance is the cost of everything it does. The dash is the compensation — further and it keeps its frames, so the forward option is the dash rather than the walk.",
